From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pinctrl: add Ingenic GPIO bias compat shim

The shared per-camera GPIO fragments in configs/cameras/<board>/<board>.dtsi
are written for the Ingenic vendor trees and #include
<dt-bindings/pinctrl/ingenic-pinctrl.h> plus the vendor GPIO bias macros
(INGENIC_GPIO_NOBIAS/PULLUP/PULLDOWN) as a third GPIO cell. The mainline
tree has neither the header nor the third cell, so every such fragment
fails to compile.

Provide the header with the vendor bias selectors defined empty. The
three-cell vendor form then collapses to the two-cell mainline form
(<&gpa pin GPIO_ACTIVE_*>), so the same fragment compiles on both, with
the bias left at the pin's reset default.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/pinctrl/ingenic-pinctrl.h
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
+/*
+ * Ingenic pinctrl/GPIO DT bindings, mainline compatibility shim.
+ *
+ * The Ingenic vendor trees (3.10/4.4) describe a GPIO as three cells:
+ *
+ *	<&gpa pin GPIO_ACTIVE_* INGENIC_GPIO_NOBIAS>
+ *
+ * where the third cell is a pin bias selector. The mainline pinctrl-ingenic
+ * binding is two cells (<&gpa pin GPIO_ACTIVE_*>); the bias is a pinctrl
+ * property rather than a GPIO flag.
+ *
+ * The shared per-camera GPIO fragments in every camera profile directory are
+ * written in the vendor three-cell form and #include this header. Defining the vendor
+ * bias selectors empty makes those fragments expand to the two-cell mainline
+ * form when built against mainline, while the vendor trees keep their own
+ * valued definitions. The bias is then left at the pin's reset default.
+ */
+#ifndef __DT_BINDINGS_INGENIC_PINCTRL_H__
+#define __DT_BINDINGS_INGENIC_PINCTRL_H__
+
+#define INGENIC_GPIO_NOBIAS
+#define INGENIC_GPIO_PULLUP
+#define INGENIC_GPIO_PULLDOWN
+
+#endif /* __DT_BINDINGS_INGENIC_PINCTRL_H__ */
